Package: scaleL
Title: Bayesian Imputation of Likert Scale Length for Meta-Analysis
Version: 0.1.0
Authors@R: c(
    person("Piers", "Steel", role = c("aut", "cre"),
           email = "piers.steel@ucalgary.ca"),
    person("Hadi", "Fariborzi", role = "aut",
           email = "hfaribor@ucalgary.ca"))
Description: Implements the Bayesian imputation procedure of Steel and
    Fariborzi (2026) for recovering missing Likert scale length L in
    meta-analytic data sets. Uses a variance-bound profile likelihood
    combined with a structured prior over L (generic, field-specific,
    instrument-specific, or user-supplied) to produce per-study posteriors,
    multiple imputations, and pooled random-effects estimates via Rubin's
    rules. Designed as a lightweight drop-in for downstream meta-analysis
    workflows.
